  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Abra Earthquake - Supporting Access to Shelter and Hygiene</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 27 July 2022, a 7.0-magnitude earthquake hit the Abra Province in northern Philippines, affecting over 136,000 families. The most affected was the Abra Province which hosts 47,653 families that are displaced and 22,633 families with totally or partially damaged houses. Damages were also reported on public infrastructures such as health facilities, schools, public roads and communication networks, limiting communities&#x2019; access to essential services and humanitarian assistance. The loss of income, livelihoods, and assets, as well as socioeconomic breakdown due to the Earthquake has taken a toll on communities&#x2019; capacity to meet basic needs. IOM seeks to mitigate the adverse effects from Earthquake Abra and displacement situations on the most vulnerable, affected communities to provision of relief items addressing the outstanding, immediate needs of Shelter and Hygiene.</narrative>
  </description>
